System Architecture
The Weather Detection System follows a simple embedded system architecture consisting of input, processing, output, and storage components.
The system is designed to collect environmental data, process it, and present meaningful information to users.

Architecture Components
Input Layer
The input section contains environmental sensors used for data collection:
Temperature Sensor – measures atmospheric temperature
Humidity Sensor – detects moisture levels in the air
Rainfall Sensor – measures rainfall conditions
These sensors continuously collect environmental information and send it to the processing unit.

Processing Layer
The microcontroller acts as the processing unit of the system.
It receives sensor signals, processes the collected data, and converts raw measurements into readable values.

Output Layer
Processed information is displayed using an LCD screen for real-time monitoring.

Storage Layer
The storage module records collected weather data for future analysis and monitoring purposes.
